/lang/ast/ast-nodes
/lang/ast/decl
/lang/ast/module
/lang/ast/row-range

+ TypeId is U32

+ no-type TypeId = U32.max
+ invalid-type TypeId = 0

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
+ TypeData is Union

| type-invalid InvalidType
| type-class ClassType
| type-variable VariableType
| type-inference InferenceType
| type-tuple TupleType
| type-struct StructType
| type-union UnionType
| type-named-union NamedUnionType
| type-function FunctionType
| type-result ResultType
| type-associated AssociatedType
| type-closure ClosureType
| type-binding BindingType

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
+ Runner is Interface

` What is checking an instance right now. The type pass keeps the runners in a stack so a
` closure called from another function is checked under the function that defines it.

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
+ IdleKit is Interface

` What a checker is made of that a type pass keeps once the checker is done, for the next
` (`TypingScratch.idle`).

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
+ TypeNode is Tuple

+ module ModuleId
+ decl DeclId

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
+ InvalidType is TypeNode

+ reason Atom?

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
+ ClassType is TypeNode

+ args RowRange'TypeId
+ errors RowRange'TypeId

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
+ TupleType is TypeNode

+ fields RowRange'TypeId
+ names RowRange'Atom

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
+ FunctionType is TypeNode

+ return-type TypeId
+ args RowRange'TypeId
+ errors RowRange'TypeId
+ is-c Bool

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
+ VariableType is TypeNode

+ index U32
+ name Atom

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
+ InferenceType is TypeNode

+ scope U32
+ ordinal U32

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
+ StructType is TypeNode

+ fields RowRange'TypeId
+ names RowRange'Atom

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
+ UnionType is TypeNode

+ cases RowRange'TypeId

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
+ NamedUnionType is TypeNode

` A union whose cases are named, for the declaration it is named for. One private to what makes it
` is told apart by the module that makes it and its place there, which are none for any other: a
` state machine's number among the machines of the module.

+ owner Atom
+ cases RowRange'TypeId
+ names RowRange'Atom
+ made-in U32 = 0
+ made-at U32 = 0

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
+ ResultType is TypeNode

+ value TypeId
+ errors RowRange'TypeId

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
+ ClosureType is TypeNode

+ enclosing U32

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
+ BindingForm is U32

` What a binding calls when it has all its arguments: a function or method by the name of its
` declaration, a constructor of its object, its object as a closure, or its object as a value
` of a function type.
| bound-function = 0
| bound-method = 1
| bound-constructor = 2
| bound-closure = 3
| bound-c-function = 4
| bound-value = 5

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
+ BindingType is TypeNode

` The explicit type arguments come first in the items, then the argument types bound so far.
` The scope is the module the binding was made in, whose overloads a call of it chooses from.
+ form BindingForm
+ scope ModuleId
+ object TypeId
+ param-count U32
+ items RowRange'TypeId

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
+ AssociatedType is TypeNode

+ owner TypeId
+ name Atom
+ args RowRange'TypeId


━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
+ DeclRef is Tuple

+ module ModuleId
+ decl DeclId

────────────────────
+ get key Size

((module as Size) /lshift/ 32) /or/ (decl as Size)

────────────────────
+ refers-to Bool
    - module ModuleId
    - decl DeclId

` Whether this is the declaration `decl` of `module`.
this.module == module && this.decl == decl

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
+ same-decl Bool
    - left DeclRef
    - right DeclRef

left.module == right.module && left.decl == right.decl

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
+ BuiltinClasses is Tuple

` The classes of core with members the compiler answers itself: `Optional`'s `value` and
` `has-value`, `TypeInfo`'s `name` and `key`, and `Number`'s `unit`.

+ optional DeclRef
+ type-info DeclRef
+ number DeclRef

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
+ CompletionState is U32

| completion-unstarted = 0
| completion-in-progress = 1
| completion-done = 2
| completion-failed = 3

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
+ storage-name String
    - storage StorageKind

match storage
    |= .storage-eager
        "eager"
    |= .storage-lazy
        "lazy"
    ??
        "getter"

